WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
This may as well be the famed battle on Gojou Bridge.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:21.500
A battle between the knife-wielding Benkei
 and the knife-wielding Ushiwakamaru!

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.500
Here's my twist!

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.850
It smells spicy, but meltingly tender.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.510
What a unique, smoky fragrance.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.970
That's bacon!

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.360
But if he's trying to match Yukihira,

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.050
he'd be using oxtail in his stew.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.680
What's the bacon for, then?

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.690
<i>Bacon in beef stew can only mean one thing.</i>

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.940
<i>He means to use it as garniture.</i>

00:00:51.030 --> 00:02:20.990
{OP}

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:15.680
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:22.150
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.900
An endless journey

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.910
Let's hone each other's pride

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.410
Words aren't really important

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.910
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:42.880
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.760
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.510
We're reckless challengers

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:55.510
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.060
A swordsman should use his blade

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.890
To open the way to the future

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:06.610
This is my story and no one else's

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:29.460
Yukihira Souma, your recipe is intended for a beef stew that has been strained.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:33.540
That'd make the dish a dull one,
 consisting of only sauce and meat.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.400
<i>And that's why the garnish,
 or garniture, becomes crucial.</i>

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.420
<i>Beef stew is said to have evolved
 from beef bourguignon,</i>

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.880
<i>a stewed beef dish with red wine from the Bourgogne region in France.</i>

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.890
<i>It also always comes with garniture,</i>

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.960
<i>usually croutons,</i>

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.000
<i>glazed pearl onions,</i>

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.000
<i>sauteed mushrooms,</i>

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.400
<i>and bacon.</i>

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.690
The smell sure is mouth-watering.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.360
It's mellow, yet so striking!

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.820
He used mesquite wood to smoke the bacon.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.440
It's a tree in the legume family
 originally found in South America.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.580
It's virtually unknown in Japan as a wood used for smoking meats.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.660
In Texas, home of barbecue,

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.750
it's one of their favorite smoking wood chips.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.770
Because of its sharp smell,

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.880
it's used to smoke meats with strong flavor,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.260
imparting a bright, golden color.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.280
In the brine,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.140
I used sage, nutmeg, and bay leaf,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.480
as well as my secret ingredient, brown sugar!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.440
The umami will be remarkably enhanced.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:37.400
Was Mimasaka that knowledgeable about smoking and curing?

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.280
His knowledge and expertise
 are on par with Ibusaki's!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.390
What's going on?!

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.780
Asshole...

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.780
Yukihira-kun doesn't seem to be going for anything unusual with his garnish.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.910
He probably didn't think of it as anything more than something on the side.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.540
Huh?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.120
Garnish, garnish.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.340
The garniture is a critical 
component of beef stews too.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.590
How disappointing.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.550
Yukihira Souma cannot win!

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:06.040
Leaping to conclusions before even
 tasting his dish... Oh, how distasteful.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.760
Having someone like you as the head chef
 must make the kitchen very tense.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.100
Shut up, thirty-year-old.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.040
I'm not thirty yet!

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.290
I'm in my twenties!

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.570
Cut it out with the cute act!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.760
Tsunozaki, you can't bring up age 
to someone's face.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.700
'Kay, I understand, Fuyumi-senpai.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.270
Why're you being polite only to Mizuhara-senpai?!

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.540
I choose who deserves my respect.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.830
<i>Oxtail, the critical ingredient, 
was profiled by Mimasaka.</i>

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.750
<i>He then added a twist 
with his special bacon.</i>

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.710
<i>Yukihira is definitely between
 a rock and a hard place now.</i>

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.990
Wh-What should he do?

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.720
At this rate, Yukihira will...

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.550
<i>Fine, I'll quit being a chef if I lose.</i>

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.640
Yukihira-senpai...

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.600
Oh, you're Soutsuda Mitsuru.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.980
You should be more careful 
with your passwords.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.190
Using your birthday's a bit too obvious.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.490
<i>I'm going to tell the entire campus about
 Yukihira-senpai's victory with my special edition!</i>

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:11.700
You saw my notes?!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.750
You really made my work easy.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.170
It's all thanks to you.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.920
<i>All the days Yukihira-senpai
 spent testing his recipes...</i>

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.530
<i>All that time he spent 
trying to be innovative...</i>

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.600
<i>Mimasaka got all that information.</i>

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.050
<i>And it's my fault.</i>

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.100
<i>That's...</i>

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.480
Tsunozaki Taki-senpai, was it?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.350
Huh?{TLC - added}

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.360
I think you've been saying 
a lot of things about me,

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.360
but I'll hear your complaints...

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.320
after I've served my dish!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.070
Those are...

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:45.950
...a lot of different...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.700
...meat...

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.320
...parts!

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:48.450
Beef cheeks.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.320
Beef tongues.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.200
Tripe!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:50.830
Fillet!

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.540
So...

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.750
dear judges,

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:59.500
I will now spirit you away 
to a meat theme park!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.920
<i>Parboil the beef tongue and peel it!</i>

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.590
He's fast!

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:08.480
<i>Brown the meat with butter for mildness,</i>

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.640
<i>plus olive oil for freshness of flavor!</i>

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.720
<i>Marinate the cheeks with red wine, parsley stalks, and bay leaves.</i>

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.230
<i>Season with salt and pepper,</i>

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.230
<i>dust the meat with a thin layer of flour,
 and then brown it!</i>

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.360
<i>Use the oven to braise the fillet, still in the pot!</i>

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.330
What?!

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.210
What's he doing?!

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.780
It means he's improvising 
everything on the fly.{kinda redundant}

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.210
Improv cooking...

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.440
The skirt steak's being...

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:32.660
Oh!

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.660
What the hell?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.160
Is he running away?!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:36.930
Oh!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.500
He's coming back.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:43.170
Oh, I'm glad I brought my clay cooking stove to the standby room.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.630
Using a clay cooking stove for beef stew?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.630
What's his game plan?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.550
He's really just putting the dish
 together right now.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.350
I see, Yukihira.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.970
Like I thought, 
that's the approach you chose to take.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.160
Opponents who know about my perfect profiling take one of two approaches.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.150
One is to put up a front,
 then try to deceive me.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.270
They first announce what dish they'll make before the match,

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:09.240
then try to confuse me by making a different dish at the match.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:14.620
The other one, which is likely the more 
confident the opponent is about their skills,

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.560
is improv cooking!

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.770
They show up without a single plan, 
then start cooking.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.330
As long as they don't think of anything, they think I won't read their thoughts.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.750
Well, the majority of them give in to panic

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.090
and lose without even 
producing a finished dish,

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.950
but I bet you'd be able to 
serve a pretty good dish.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.320
You're not the type to panic midway.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.850
Why're you praising me all of a sudden?

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.010
I've put my trust in you.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.560
I know everything about you.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.360
I know you went by Aldini's
 apartment this morning,

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:50.610
and I know you got 
a ton of meat after that.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.200
We will first evaluate Mimasaka Subaru's dish.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:08:01.030
Well, enjoy.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:06.520
He used bacon, mushrooms, and glazed pearl onions as the garniture.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:10.840
The french word for glazed,
 "glacé," means to freeze.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.380
The glossy surface, like ice,
 visually pulls the dish together.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.040
Shut up!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.390
Just dig in already!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.010
I... I will.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:28.630
<i>The oxtail's viscosity and the mild white miso hidden deep within are exquisite!</i>

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:32.360
I think my tongue's melting apart!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:37.420
<i>And yet, the fragrance of mesquite from the bacon strikes a powerful note!</i>

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:38.950
It's unbelievably delicious!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.890
I've predicted all your thoughts.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.460
I knew you'd spring for improv cooking too.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.350
That's why I went for this special bacon!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:50.680
It spent a whole five days in the brine!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.630
I air-dried it for a whole day,

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.260
then smoked it for five hours.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:00.510
That's how much time and effort this level of umami requires.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.030
Indeed...

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.680
The umami of this carefully-nurtured pork

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:08.480
serves not to undermine, but instead to heighten the beef's flavor!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.320
The time and effort this required... the weight of it!

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:15.990
This dish possesses a strength that can be considered the total opposite of an improv dish!

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.420
It's just like what happened in Takumi-cchi's match!

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:21.290
He even knew that Souma-kun
 would try improv cooking.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.450
He predicted everything.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:24.830
He made a preemptive move!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.960
So light! So tender!

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.840
This flavor goes far beyond the
 realm of possibility with profiling.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.050
This is as though...

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:38.080
there is a fierce clash between meats in the fighting ring!

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.970
This extreme deliciousness 
shakes you to the very bone!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.440
<i>No! I can't contain it all!</i>

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.900
The interplay between beef and pork...

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.360
Their cross-impact!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.570
High praise!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.320
Even the professional chefs are in awe!

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:12.040
How foolish, Yukihira!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:16.260
Building a dish on the fly
 as inspiration strikes you...

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:21.470
It may sound like a great idea at first glance, but it's nothing other than blanking out!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:25.640
Those who plan their cooking
 right down to the last detail

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.770
and make the necessary 
preparations always win!

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:34.320
No matter how many tricks you may try to hide up your sleeve, it's useless!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.990
It's all pointless!

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.570
Well, don't ever forget this moment.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:46.150
It's the last dish you'll 
ever serve to a customer.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.670
You say that like I don't know you, Mimasaka.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.840
See, I put my trust in <i>you</i> as well.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:02.640
What?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:07.640
I also thought about you all last week.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.980
<i>No matter what he may try to pull,</i>

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.770
<i>it should fall within my range of predictions.</i>

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>And yet... why am I afraid?</i>

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.360
Well, here you go.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.490
Enjoy!

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.080
It's the Yukihira-Style Beef Stew—

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.330
the Autumn Election Special!

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.080
What?

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.920
So many different meat parts!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.500
This'd better not be a joke.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.960
I've never seen a beef stew like thi—

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.380
What do you mean?

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.510
It <i>is</i> beef stew.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.430
That's all just garniture.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.050
What?!

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.850
That's all garnish?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.930
The smoky fragrance of charcoal...

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.680
It's cooked just right.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.440
<i>Hmph.</i>

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.190
<i>Shoving random ingredients
 together into a mish-mash...</i>

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.150
<i>Talk about a crude attempt!</i>

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:02.110
<i>It could hardly live up to my garniture.</i>

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:06.410
<i>I nurtured my special bacon with the alluring smell of mesquite.</i>

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:10.330
<i>He can't compete with my 
meticulously-cultivated flavor.</i>

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.830
Hm.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:16.210
The stew itself is not that different 
from the one we just had.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.090
As for the garniture...

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:29.770
<i>What?!</i>

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.390
<i>Right!</i>

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.350
<i>Left!</i>

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.360
<i>And a surprising loop!</i>

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.230
Delicious!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.200
The meltingly tender cheeks 
fall apart when you bite in!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.950
The tongue and tripe offer 
great texture and mouthfeel!

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.540
The charcoal-grilled skirt steak

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.910
is unbelievably juicy because of its thick cut!

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.920
Even when tasted with the stew,

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.170
the garniture adds a great accent to the dish.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.420
Indeed.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.010
This may seem slapdash at first glance,

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.220
but each component has been 
precisely prepared.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.890
It is an attraction that has 
been carefully composed.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:09.680
It is perfectly balanced.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.310
Impossible!

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.980
How could he improvise that?!

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.600
To be honest,

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.310
I was thinking along 
the same lines as you.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.570
About using a strongly flavored garniture 
like smoked bacon to strengthen the flavor.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.990
But that wouldn't be right.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.200
That wouldn't be my style of cooking.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:32.120
I wanted something where a wide range of flavors and ingredients

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.870
would gather into a single dish.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:40.590
I never thought beef stew could have so much depth and range of flavor.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:45.090
Oh, well, my thinking 
was inspired by a certain dish.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.550
What dish?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.050
I only had that flash of inspiration
 this morning, but yeah.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.800
It was the Chikuzen stew.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:51.760
Huh?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:55.060
The dish is commonly 
misinterpreted as a simple stew,

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:58.270
but when it's made by a professional,
 it's something else.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.730
Right, Hinako-senpai?

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:00.900
Yes.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:06.450
By simmering each vegetable ingredient 
separately for the optimal amount of time,

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.700
you can maximize each 
ingredient's color and flavor.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.910
Then you reassemble 
the components into the final dish,

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:16.330
while paying minute attention to the balance of ingredients.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.710
This dish is the same.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.290
Chikuzen stew... 
that's definitely a dish of the people.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.170
That's Yukihira's specialty!

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:27.630
Yukihira, weren't you just doing improv cooking without any pre-planning?!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.090
I never said it was improv.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.140
I've been building this dish for my entire life!

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.600
The path I had to take to get to this point...

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.400
The countless flavor combinations I've tried...

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:46.820
I called on everything I had to 
create the dish in my head.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.780
You've always only taken 
the one step necessary

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:52.660
to surpass the recipe you stole 
from your opponent.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.830
I thought you wouldn't be able
 to do what I was attempting.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:59.500
<i>An approach my perfect profiling cannot reach?!</i>

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.460
<i>What he built</i>

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.750
<i>is a paradise decorated with all the delicious flavors beef has to offer.</i>

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.840
<i>A land of dreams that makes 
you want to stay forever.</i>

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.470
<i>Beloved by all!</i>

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.180
Yukihee Land!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:32.530
Hey.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.660
Let's remember today forever.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:39.370
Yeah!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.250
Let's all be friends forever!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.130
Let go of me!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.550
Taki-chan, you have small, cute hands.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.300
What?!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.810
Why are you all teary-eyed?!

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.810
So cute!

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:00.810
It seems Yukihira was the one who didn't blank out in the end.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.810
Stop staring! Go back to your seat already!

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.860
The long, long history 
of pursuing your own cooking...

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.820
That is the depth possessed 
by a professional chef.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.860
Yukihira has concentrated all of that most admirably into a single dish!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.580
We'll now enter the final assessment.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.000
This concludes the first semi-final match of the Autumn Election.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.460
and the Cooking Battle!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.380
Judges, please cast your vote!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.130
Now, what is the outcome?!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.300
Candidate Yukihira Souma 
has won the Cooking Battle

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.520
and will proceed to the finals!

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.310
Glad you liked it!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.390
He won!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.150
Souma-kun!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.400
Impossible.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.610
No one can escape my profiling!

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.740
If that's what you think,

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.240
you should taste this too.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.840
<i>Yukihee Land!</i>

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.420
<i>Shit. Why is it... so pleasant?</i>

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:18.390
<i>I'm starting to remember how it used to be</i>

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.560
<i>when I'd just started cooking!</i>

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:25.350
<i>Young Master Subaru, 
you're so clever with your hands!</i>

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:29.940
<i>You can recreate any dish
 just by glancing at the recipe!</i>

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.650
<i>You're your father's son, for sure.</i>

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.030
<i>What wonderful talent!</i>

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.110
<i>You're making me feel embarrassed.</i>

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.120
<i>This is just me learning by imitation.</i>

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:44.080
<i>Would Dad praise me if he sees this?</i>

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:46.540
<i>Don't be so happy over this poor imitation!</i>

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:52.000
<i>A truly top-notch chef stands out with his own unique, personal style!</i>

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.760
<i>This restaurant has no need for chefs who have no personal creed!</i>

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.630
<i>A few days later,</i>

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:01.350
<i>there was a showcase of our new dishes with a lot of VIP customers in attendance.</i>

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:03.810
<i>I didn't do it out of malice.</i>

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.600
<i>I just wanted his respect.</i>

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:11.060
<i>I added just one simple twist 
to Dad's specialty dish,</i>

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.070
<i>and I won.</i>

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.200
<i>I was exiled.</i>

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.490
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.330
<i>Dad ran away from me.</i>

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:25.450
<i>Oh... cooking's easy.</i>

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:26.910
<i>Just one step...</i>

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.210
<i>One small step is all I need 
to surpass my opponents.</i>

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.380
<i>I have that talent!</i>

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.750
<i>Look, see?</i>

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.880
<i>All the elites at Japan's 
elite culinary academy</i>

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.340
<i>are at their wits' end and losing to me.</i>

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.560
<i>Top-notch? Creed?</i>

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.140
<i>Yeah, right. 
Worthless chefs!</i>

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:51.100
<i>Mimasaka Subaru... you are useful.</i>

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.980
<i>Come work for me.</i>

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.820
<i>I'll let you wreak whatever havoc you want.</i>

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:02.910
With this Cooking Battle,

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:08.330
Mimasaka Subaru has lost 
all rights to these tools.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.710
Yukihira Souma, I understand you wish 
to return all of them to their former owners.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.040
Is that correct?

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.170
Yup!

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:27.100
Ah! One hundred knives are being
 returned to their chefs!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.600
Um, Yukihira-kun.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:36.020
This knife belonged to my mom. I got it when she passed away.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.860
Thank you.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.650
Thank you so much.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.450
It's time.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.660
I'll leave Tohtsuki.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.870
I won't cook anymore.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.920
I suffered such a miserable defeat.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.000
There's nothing left for me to be proud of—

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.500
Idiot!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:59.880
Why did I accept your Cooking 
Battle challenge, then?

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.430
Hey, what's the matter?

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.550
Aren't you going to claim it?

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.810
The last one's yours, Takumi.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.690
Aldini...

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.440
Mimasaka Subaru.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.070
I lost to you.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.650
It was total defeat.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.860
But next time, I won't lose!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.660
If you're one step ahead of me,

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.080
I'll take two... no, ten... a hundred steps!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.240
I won't let things end this way.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:30.700
Do you hear me, Mimasaka?!

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.210
The mezzaluna is now Yukihira's.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.710
I will get it back someday...

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.630
after I beat you in a Cooking Battle!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.420
Until then, keep it safe for me!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.430
See?

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:49.430
People who want to become professional chefs

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.680
are all really sore losers.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.140
Listen up, Mimasaka.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:21:00.280
Never plan to take your opponent's entire pride in a single match ever again.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.240
Even if all the confidence and pride you've built over the years

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.570
is blown to pieces by a major failure...

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.200
Even if you've had a soul-crushing experience...

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.450
you still have to open shop the next day.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.460
That's who chefs are.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.420
Aren't you the same way?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.340
Mimasaka?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:25.260
<i>Is he telling me to keep on 
cooking, despite who I am?</i>

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:31.100
<i>My cold, hardened heart...</i>

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:35.270
<i>is softening again.</i>

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.810
<i>I have cuticles like a girl!</i>

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:44.650
You decided to put your 
life as a chef on the line

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.200
to send a message about
 starting over, even if you lose?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.570
It doesn't make a whole lot of sense.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.200
Yeah, you're right.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.700
But it's something Souma-kun would do.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:56.040
Hey, Nakiri.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.120
I managed to get this far.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:02.090
Just one more step until I get to where I can face off with you

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.710
as the top first-year.

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.260
Know your place.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.590
I am far above and beyond where you are!

00:22:12.060 --> 00:23:42.020
{ED}

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:41.170
An intensely burning desire was born

00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:47.010
But not in me, in someone else

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:51.810
Where's the me who believed that

00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:56.940
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:02.190
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:07.950
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:13.290
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:18.460
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:24.130
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:29.180
You can call it resignation if you want

00:23:29.180 --> 00:23:35.100
But that's not me, that's not me

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:39.730
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:23:42.730 --> 00:23:43.860
Also...

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:46.690
don't forget to bring me that book.

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:52.410
We'll now proceed to the second
 match of the semi-finals!

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:58.950
We have Candidate Kurokiba Ryou and Candidate Hayama Akira!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:10.050
Next time, "Beasts Devouring Each Other."
